//! The formatter's idioms for this feature — `rule`s, reached by
//! this feature's `mod.av`, the way any declaration is.
use features.{Fix, rule}

/// A name imported and never used ANYWHERE in its MODULE — never
/// per FILE, since bs2 merges a module's own files into one bundle,
/// so an import in one file may serve another (`program.av`'s import
/// can be `mod.av`'s to use); a per-file scan deletes an import a
/// sibling still depends on. The compiler refuses a MISSING import
/// (F3000) and one a module does not export (F3012); an unused one
/// is silent, so this rule keeps that direction.
/// `unused_imports()`/`unused_import_decls()` (features/code.av, THE
/// REFERENCES RELATION) already exempt a component instance
/// (`DeclFacts.instance`): its use is being REACHABLE for a
/// `collect`, not being read.
///
/// A `Fix.Delete`: the item is dropped from its `use` line, well-
/// formed either way — the line rewritten around whatever else it
/// still names, or gone whole when nothing survives it
/// (`compiler/rule_delete.av`'s `use_line_edits`). NO `@fixes`
/// EXAMPLE: a lone example file names no package
/// (`imported_line`'s own `self.lone` door), so a `use` line inside
/// one never resolves to an import row at all — there is no
/// scratch-file shape this fires on. `compiler/tests/
/// rule_fix_test.av` and the tree's own dogfooding (`avra fix` over
/// a real package) prove the delete itself.
@keeps("1 + 1")
@law("an import nothing anywhere reads changes no program it stands over")
export rule unused_import { quote { ${u} } if !u.unused_imports().is_empty() -> Fix.Delete(u.unused_import_decls()) }
